   $q$The height of a sunflower seedling, in centimeters, is $h(w) = 1.5w + 4$, where $w$ is the number of weeks after planting. Which statement correctly interprets $h(6) = 13$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After 13 weeks, the seedling is 6 centimeters tall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-input-and-output"},{"text":"The seedling grows 13 centimeters each week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-value-with-rate"},{"text":"After 6 weeks, the seedling is 13 centimeters tall.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The seedling grows 6 centimeters in 13 weeks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"read-values-as-change"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After 6 weeks, the seedling is 13 centimeters tall.$q$, $q$The input $w = 6$ is the time in weeks and the output $13$ is the height, and indeed $1.5(6) + 4 = 13$. The rate of growth is $1.5$ centimeters per week, so reading $13$ as a weekly rate confuses a value with a rate.$q$, 'draft', null)
